:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, a scheduled restart, a different post-restart boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered chronyd/configuration and synchronization state.","limitations":["Restart acknowledgements were shell-level scheduling confirmations rather than provider-native acknowledgement records, although connectivity interruption and changed boot identities directly confirm that both restarts occurred.","Lifecycle collection provides only bounded inventories and does not independently capture chrony configuration or firewall contents; those states are established by executor command output.","Executor-created diagnostic files and rollback copies were not cleaned up."]}
